        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Sarkozy trial 'test to French judicial system' when faced with political pressure France Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 16:54 Modified: 16/03/2026 - 16:56 Former French president Nicolas Sarkozy is on trial once again as he appeals his conviction in the Libyan funding case. Although a guilty verdict is unlikely to change what his base thinks of him, it would undeniably taint his legacy. The trial also sends out a clear message to the political elite over corruption and is a robustness test for the country's judicial system, as FRANCE 24's Camille Knight reports. 'Hard to draw conclusions for presidential election' from French municipal vote 16/03/2026 France Sarkozy's high-stakes appeal in Libyan funding case opens in Paris 16/03/2026 France What to know from the first round of France's municipal elections 16/03/2026 France Former president Sarkozy appeals conviction in Libyan funding case 16/03/2026 France 44% abstention: French local elections 'poorly attended dress rehearsal' for 2027 presidential race 16/03/2026 France Paris looks at five-way race for new mayor 16/03/2026 France Far-right and left make major gains across France in mayoral election 16/03/2026 France Voter turnout reaches 48.90% in France's first round of local elections 15/03/2026 France French parties test strategies in municipal elections ahead of 2027 presidential poll 15/03/2026 France"
