        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russia is 'country that benefits most the longer Middle East war continues' Middle East Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 16:48 Modified: 16/03/2026 - 16:49 Donald Trump is putting pressure on European countries to keep Strait of Hormuz open. But as Europe refuses to get dragged into the war in the Middle East, it also doesn't want to jeopardise Ukraine, which benefits from the US in different ways. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley looks at how the two conflicts are intertwined. Europe refuses to join Middle East war, weighs options to secure Strait of Hormuz 16/03/2026 Middle East Possibility of long war source of concern Israeli military leaders 16/03/2026 Middle East Middle East conflict is not NATO war, but 'entwined' with US position on Ukraine 16/03/2026 Middle East Trump presses China, says NATO faces 'very bad' future if allies don't help open Hormuz Strait 16/03/2026 Middle East 16/03/2026 Middle East UK won't commit soldiers to a war without 'legal basis' amid Trump threats 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli forces kill four in a car in West Bank 16/03/2026 Middle East Answering Trump's call for help in Middle East 'political suicide' for allies 16/03/2026 Middle East IDF launches 'limited operation' in Lebanon as 'buffer zone expands significantly' 16/03/2026 Middle East"
